\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every compact smooth positively curved surface Sigma in $R^3$, allowing a smooth boundary, and every $p>3$, is its surface extension operator bounded from $L^p(Sigma)$ to $L^p(R^3)$?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every compact smooth positively curved surface Sigma in $R^3$, allowing a smooth boundary, and every $p>3$, is its surface extension operator bounded from $L^p(Sigma)$ to $L^p(R^3)$?

